Chapter: CapDirection

 This opening declares FileSystem.Read and nothing else of that family.
 It reads its own capability word back out of the process table and
 reports the two filesystem bits: read is bit 6, write is bit 7.

   read=1 write=0   the row was honoured. The only passing answer.
   read=1 write=1   direction was ignored and the program was handed an
                    authority it never asked for. That is what this test
                    exists to catch, and it is what the machine did
                    before today.
   read=0           the grant was lost entirely; a program that declared
                    the effect cannot use it.

Section: Bits

  cap-bit : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  cap-bit (word) (n) = if bit-and word (bit-shl 1 n) /= 0 then 1 else 0

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console, FileSystem.Read] Nothing
  opening = act
    print-line-uni ("fs-read "  & show (cap-bit (process-get-cap process-get-pid) 6))
    print-line-uni ("fs-write " & show (cap-bit (process-get-cap process-get-pid) 7))
    print-line-uni ("con-read "  & show (cap-bit (process-get-cap process-get-pid) 4))
    print-line-uni ("con-write " & show (cap-bit (process-get-cap process-get-pid) 5))
  end
